From 6e18c2fb411d645ffc0bb80300599be4af21a7bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:27:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 132/137] wifi: ath11k: Keep a user's country that 11d had
 already set

A user regulatory hint for the country the phy already has (typically
one 11d found in the beacons a moment earlier) returned without doing
anything: 11d stayed on and could later replace the user's choice, and
ar->alpha2 kept 11d's code. Treat it like any other user setting: stop
the 11d scan, mark the regdomain as set by the user and keep the code to
send again after a firmware restart (resume). No WMI command is needed,
the firmware already runs that country.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
index 6bae8d1906c9..e4b12727806b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
@@ -87,6 +87,13 @@ ath11k_reg_notifier(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct regulatory_request *request)
 
 	if (!ath11k_regdom_changes(ar, request->alpha2)) {
 		ath11k_dbg(ar->ab, ATH11K_DBG_REG, "Country is already set\n");
+		/* 11d may have set the same country: from now on it is the
+		 * user's, which 11d does not change and a firmware restart
+		 * gets again.
+		 */
+		memcpy(&ar->alpha2, request->alpha2, 2);
+		ath11k_mac_11d_scan_stop(ar);
+		ar->regdom_set_by_user = true;
 		return;
 	}
 
